      "extract": "arXiv:0905.0228v4 [math.CO] 17 Jun 2010 A CURIOUS q-ANALOGUE OF HERMITE POLYNOMIALS JOHANN CIGLER AND JIANG ZENG Abstract. Two well-known q-Hermite polynomials are the continuous and discrete q-Hermite polynomials. In this paper we consider a new family of q-Hermite polynomials and prove several curious properties about these polynomials. One striking property is the connection with q-Fibonacci and q-Lucas",
      "extractCut": true,
