      "extract": "There are many ways to construct Hermite polynomials. For example, the normalized Hermite polynomials $H_n(x,s)=s^{n/2}H_n(x/\\sqrt{s}, 1)$ ($n\\geq 0$) may be defined by the recurrence relation: \\begin{align}\\label{eq:rec1} H_{n+1}(x,s)=xH_n(x,s)-nsH_{n-1}(x,s), \\end{align} with initial values $H_0(x,s)=1$ and $H_{-1}(x,s)=0$. By induction, we have \\begin{align}\\label{eq:op} H_n(x,s)=(x-s{\\D})^n\\cdot 1, \\end{align}",
      "extractCut": true
