      "extract": "We define the Lucas polynomials by $$ l_n(x,s)=xl_{n-1}(x,s)+sl_{n-2}(x,s)\\quad \\text{for}�\\quad n>2, $$ with initial values $l_1(x,s)=x$ and $l_2(x,s)=x^2+2s$. They have the explicit formula \\begin{align}\\label{eq:luc1} l_n(x,s)=\\sum_{2k\\leq n} \\frac{n}{n-k} {n-k\\choose k}s^k x^{n-2k} \\quad (n>0). \\end{align} Furthermore we define $l_0(x,s)=1$. Note that this definition differs from the usual one in which",
