      "extract": "Theorem 5 and the orthogonality of the continuous q-Hermite polynomials. Clearly Theorem 5 is equivalent to xn = X k≡n (mod 2) c(n, k, q)s(n−k)/2 ˜Hk(x, s|q). (5.14) To compute c(n, k, q) we can take s = 1 and let ˜Hn(x|q) = ˜Hn(x, s|q). It is known (see [9]) that the continuous q-Hermite polynomials ( ˜Hn(x|q)) are orthogonal with respect to the linear functional ϕ deﬁned by ϕ(xn) = Z 2/√1−q −2/√1−q xnv(x, q)dx,",
